0..42 Comment "/// A derived filler owes a model nothing."
43..46 Comment "///"
47..115 Comment "/// Completion derives the associator of four from a monoid\'s binary"
116..191 Comment "/// associativity and proves it for every model. So a model writes only its"
192..213 Comment "/// rules\' witnesses."
214..217 Comment "///"
218..297 Comment "/// The `derive` declaration states the associator, and a model reads it as the"
298..377 Comment "/// theory\'s member `Monoid.assoc4`. Both sides rewrite to one normal form, and"
378..409 Comment "/// the rewrites are the proof."
410..413 Comment "///"
414..493 Comment "/// - see: #4106 — a component a model writes for a derived filler is refused"
494..572 Comment "/// - see: `pathological/identity/derived-associator.gandr` — the model that"
573..604 Comment "///   writes the associator too"
605..679 Comment "/// - see: Knuth and Bendix, _Simple Word Problems in Universal Algebras_,"
680..711 Comment "///   1970, § 7 — completion"
